---
// §3: a short dry explainer. It ends on the same license paragraph as
// /contribute/, rendered from the one `license.body` string.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';
import { t } from '../../i18n';

const licenseParagraphs = t('license.body').split('\n\n');
---

<BaseLayout
  title={t('howItWorks.title')}
  description={`How ideas get considered, set free, and published on ${SITE.title}.`}
>
  <section class="page-head section">
    <p class="eyebrow">{t('howItWorks.eyebrow')}</p>
    <h1>Someone has an idea. Then they let it go.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      ProductUnhunt publishes ridiculous business ideas as serious analysis. The presentation is the
      joke. Nothing here is looking for funding.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-label="The process">
    <div class="feature-list process-list">
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">01</p>
        <h3>An idea is considered.</h3>
        <p>
          Usually in a shower, a queue, or the twenty minutes after a bad meeting. It survives long
          enough to be described out loud.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">02</p>
        <h3>It is set free.</h3>
        <p>
          This is the part the internet skips. An idea qualifies here only once someone has thought
          about building it and chosen not to.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">03</p>
        <h3>It gets written up in five sections.</h3>
        <p>
          The Pitch, The Delusion, The Reality Check, Why It Stays Unbuilt, and an Unwanted Bonus —
          the adjacent idea that is somehow even less buildable.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">04</p>
        <h3>The editor publishes it.</h3>
        <p>
          Anyone can submit; the editor publishes. There is no queue position, no upvote gate, and
          no algorithm deciding what surfaces.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">05</p>
        <h3>You deliver a verdict.</h3>
        <p>
          Six options, one vote per idea, changeable. No login, no likes, and no leaderboard. It is
          not election-grade and does not pretend to be.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <p class="eyebrow">06</p>
        <h3>Nobody builds it.</h3>
        <p>
          That is the whole outcome. If an idea does become real, its status changes to
          <em>Unfortunately real</em> and we all sit with that.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section license-section" aria-labelledby="license-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow" id="license-heading">{t('license.eyebrow')}</p>
    <div class="license-body">
      {licenseParagraphs.map((paragraph) => <p>{paragraph}</p>)}
    </div>
    <div class="action-row">
      <a class="button" href={withBase('/contribute/')}>{t('cta.submit')}</a>
      <a class="text-link" href={withBase('/ideas/')}>{t('cta.fullPile')}</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
